{"title":"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2024 USAMO/5</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">2024 USAJMO/6</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is selected inside acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/c/6acd00d8a9993fe8dbef8619ca092bdcadd29317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAC=\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/237c8a74e6a9d07badfb12532e8e64f7d9ef2cd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDC=90^\\circ+\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"187\" height=\"16\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen on ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cc64d695e60b2ce5256f22259d4a9dca7cd7176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=EC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Show that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72cf35ccd4cc779c3ba0c092b7f6de4bad558ff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BEM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/b/aebbcd80b53bfcf3938e0707006994c910e78e3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DBT = \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea26fb6ec15ff3993c43a02b3834d4781d8b30b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEM = \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />.  \nExtend AD intersects BC at point T, then TC = TA, TE is perpendicular to AC\n</p><p>Thus, AB is the tangent of the circle BEM\n</p><p>Then the question is equivalent as  the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a9e947ed7a758a3c7d8ccb45c839eaea7a3d316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" /> is the auxillary angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/6/0161620114b26ca59ea485e4190371790c90a1f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><i>ontinued</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f61faf2e989ce96583afbdfbc1f7930ffd086ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAC = \\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />, which implies symmetry about the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, we can extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> to intersect the circumcircle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, and by symmetry about the perpendicular bisector, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/f/40f3932b418529068fe83f207698d916d4cb7a7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABQC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> is an isoceles trapezoid. Now, we realize that the midpoint condition is annoying, which really suggests that to simplify things, we take a homothety at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> sending <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and we just need to prove that the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/b/b8bbe23a02a61206265e5042ac8b91fbf949623c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BE&#39;C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"19\" /> is tangent to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411ef29ce6c32ab71534dfd3319a6fe72af9c5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the resultant point from a homothety at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. However, funnily enough, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05c319316e2350829a3d2b300a4cd9fba795382b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AE}=\\overline{EC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />, and the perpendicular bisector gets sent to an altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> under homothety, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411ef29ce6c32ab71534dfd3319a6fe72af9c5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is simply the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> and the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />! Call that point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. We can now ignore points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Note that we have not used the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd5529f83cca44961d418dc5a92baf90a667913c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> condition yet, which means we should probably try angle chasing now. Call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7624b257eee9cf756b27ccd1f1e55290f7d22b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC=a, \\angle ABC = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" />. By angle condition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97df16788197059f7306645cd81cfac150db37e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDC = 90+a, \\angle CDP = 90-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"273\" height=\"18\" />. Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/e/8cede23795ae600af1bc3a15a59a82bdecb7623b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle QCA = \\angle BAC = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/3179f700f28477353045fbb131fd63e28b48f140.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PQC = 90 - \\angle ACQ = 90-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"252\" height=\"18\" />. A miracle occurs! <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/1/941ce70bbfb7cde605095b12c70c6b9998a77535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDP = \\angle ACQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />, so quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d47ff215db5a2c8df0febfff17ab6f465f5f6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QDPC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> is cyclic! <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f45c6d3b6783d6b8731fdffc3fce9850c6b03cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = \\angle AQC = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" /> from isoceles trapezoid, and from cyclicity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/66043ba6ca7f2ac598b4ff762d466afdab7d1939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DPC = 180-b = \\angle BPC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"221\" height=\"16\" />. Now we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/f/38f7fc84e5adf90f778a365cb8aa9d7b83584070.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/deb0d6de5a3da879e4bee7d03cee1de7d47cdabf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BPC = 180-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" />, which looks a lot like tangency condition. We realize that it simply is the tangency condition if we extend line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> to get the supplementary angle, so we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yYRaQbGJpPg\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yYRaQbGJpPg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO\" title=\"2024 USAMO\">2024 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2024\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO\" title=\"2024 USAJMO\">2024 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2024\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017211714\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.082 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 331/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2453/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 201/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8913/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   40.915      1 -total\n 30.23%   12.370      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 17.00%    6.954      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 13.81%    5.649      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n 13.64%    5.579      1 Template:Duplicate\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:27283:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017211714 and revision id 274910. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}